-- Forward from a changed specification: the rule-model edits a change to the rule's packet implies.
-- Binds $model (the rule model the profile is consistent with), $before and $after (the rule's packet before and after the
-- change). Replies with node edits in the backward passes' format — change, add or remove a node — each added or changed
-- node quoting the passage of the CHANGED packet it rests on, so the model keeps its provenance. Applying them is
-- deterministic; patch-route.nlir and patch.nlir then carry them into an existing profile.
-- A changed definition edits the conditions and permissions that use its term: typed as a fact it would reach UNCERTAIN
-- only, though the term decides MET and NOT MET (edit-loop.py --impact-apply). Runs recorded before that rule was added
-- replay from the cache only with the earlier wording (this file's history).
$json%($parse%(=>("A RULE MODEL was extracted from a rule's PACKET: the behaviour judged (action), conditions that must all hold for a violation, exceptions (permissions) any one of which avoids it, facts a verdict turns on, and the testing setting. The packet has CHANGED. Find the smallest edits to the RULE MODEL that make it reflect the changed packet.\n\nRules:\n- Model only what changed; unchanged passages need no edit.\n- A new permitted case is a new permission; a new requirement for a violation is a new or narrowed condition; a new deciding unknown is a new fact; a removed passage removes the node that rested on it.\n- A changed DEFINITION changes what its term means wherever the model uses it: edit the conditions and permissions that use the term (narrowing or widening them), not only a fact.\n- Give each edited or added node the passage of the CHANGED packet it rests on, quoted exactly.\n\nReply with JSON only: {\"edits\": [{\"op\": \"edit\" | \"add\" | \"remove\", \"group\": \"action\" | \"setting\" | \"conditions\" | \"permissions\" | \"facts\", \"id\": \"<the node's id, for edit and remove>\", \"text\": \"<the node's new text, for edit and add>\", \"source\": \"<the quoted passage>\"}], \"why\": \"<one sentence>\"}\n\nRULE MODEL:\n" ++ $json%$model ++ "\n\nPACKET BEFORE:\n" ++ $json%$before ++ "\n\nPACKET AFTER:\n" ++ $json%$after)))
